# Sandcastle host settings and credentials
#
# Do NOT create .sandcastle/.env. Sandcastle forwards every key in it into the
# sandbox, whichever agent runs, so the dispatch and dispatch-waves refuse to
# start when it holds any key (ADR 0010, #1593).
#
# Where credentials come from, highest first:
#   1. A 1Password Environment, when OP_ENVIRONMENT_ID is set (recommended).
#      Its variables are read in memory on the host, never written to disk.
#   2. Your shell.
#   3. This file, copied to .sandcastle/secrets.env (gitignored, read only by
#      the host scripts, never handed to Sandcastle).
# Only the selected agent's one credential is passed into the sandbox.

# 1Password Environment id: Developer > View Environments > your Environment >
# Manage environment > Copy environment ID. Not a secret, so it may live here;
# a value in your shell wins. Put the credentials below (and any SANDCASTLE_*
# settings) in the Environment itself.
# OP_ENVIRONMENT_ID=
# Optional: path to a specific 1Password CLI binary. Under WSL the Windows
# op.exe is used automatically unless OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN is set.
# OP_CLI=

# Optional: default agent provider for dispatch.
# Supported values: claude, cursor, copilot, codex (codex is preview-only: its launch refuses until #1641)
SANDCASTLE_AGENT=claude

# Optional: default model overrides per provider.
# Claude still falls back to the issue complexity labels when this is unset.
# SANDCASTLE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# SANDCASTLE_CLAUDE_MODEL=
SANDCASTLE_CURSOR_MODEL=composer-2.5
SANDCASTLE_COPILOT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5.5

# Optional: which Claude Code the sandbox image runs. Changing either takes
# effect on the next dispatch, which rebuilds the image when its CLI differs.
#   auto   — follow the latest release; each dispatch checks for a newer one.
#   manual — stay on SANDCASTLE_CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION (an exact version).
# Unset means auto, or manual when a version is set. Each slice log names the
# version it ran.
# SANDCASTLE_CLAUDE_CODE_UPDATE=auto
# SANDCASTLE_CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION=2.1.310

# Required for Claude Code agents. Provide exactly ONE — the orchestrator forwards
# the OAuth token when both are present and drops the API key entirely, so a stale
# key can never silently take over billing.
#
#   CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN — run `claude setup-token` on the HOST (needs a Pro/Max
#     plan). Bills your subscription, which is the same quota as your interactive
#     Claude Code sessions: long AFK batches can throttle you at the keyboard.
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — metered API billing, isolated from the plan quota.
#
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=your-token-here
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-key-here

# Optional: force one auth mode instead of letting the token win.
# Fails fast if the matching credential is missing. subscription | api
# SANDCASTLE_CLAUDE_AUTH=subscription

# Required for Cursor agents.
# CURSOR_API_KEY=your-cursor-api-key

# Required for GitHub Copilot CLI agents. Only this variable is forwarded.
# Use a fine-grained personal access token with the "Copilot Requests" permission
# and NO repository access: the sandbox must never hold a token that can read or
# push code. GH_TOKEN and GITHUB_TOKEN are never forwarded into the sandbox for
# any agent, and a dispatch refuses to start if one reaches it (only the host
# pushes — ADR 0010).
# COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN=your-fine-grained-token-here
